{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade","id":1017585,"title":"Requiem and Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-15T04:24:49-08:00","id":1017585,"title":"Requiem and Masquerade","content":"What I like about Requiem: great Clans, fascinating Covenants, incredible diversity of individual Kindred in the published Citybooks<br /> <br /> What I don't like: Requiem needs more metaplot, more overarching conspiracies, more sinister elders hiding in the shadows<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, I LOVE the fluff in Requiem, but I don't like the toolbox approach, and I wish it were more like Masquerade in underlying structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. As I always remind people when I post these sorts of posts, I am a girl who loves to cause drama, and I know that writing this will probably push SOMEBODY's buttons. Still, it is really how I feel, and if I ever did run Requiem, this is pretty much how I would do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:51:09-08:00","id":1017592,"title":"","content":"Well, you're out of luck if you want all those as official, published materials. CofD focuses more on the local and the personal, both geographically and historically. It favors flexibility over stability, and the internal over the external.<br /> <br /> Of course, overarching global conspiracies and uber-elders in the dark are all doable, as long as you work towards building them yourself. Metaplot is still out, because that's by definition something the developers and the writers make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:03:36-08:00","id":1017594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade#post1017585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I like about Requiem: great Clans, fascinating Covenants, incredible diversity of individual Kindred in the published Citybooks<br /> <br /> What I don't like: Requiem needs more metaplot, more overarching conspiracies, more sinister elders hiding in the shadows<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, I LOVE the fluff in Requiem, but I don't like the toolbox approach, and I wish it were more like Masquerade in underlying structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. As I always remind people when I post these sorts of posts, I am a girl who loves to cause drama, and I know that writing this will probably push SOMEBODY's buttons. Still, it is really how I feel, and if I ever did run Requiem, this is pretty much how I would do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen</div> </div> </div> </div>Solution is simple: Create your conspiracies, create your metaplot. Danse Macabre book from first edition went a little bit into that with it's world spanning Covenant versions and all, so it <i>might</i> help. (However, I wouldn't recommend buying it since it's pretty old by now). <br /> <br /> Moreover, there's a book Thousand Years of Night which is being developed. It will delve more into old and mysterious elders. It won't help you much with a metaplot (as it won't have one), but it will give you more tools to build those ancient creatures <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:04:06-08:00","id":1017595,"title":"","content":"No metaplot and less overarching conspiracies is the whole point of Requiem so that wont happen, but a book on elders is being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:12:52-08:00","id":1017600,"title":"","content":"I am a little bit heartened by the secret of Prince Vidal's final fate being revealed in Secrets of the Covenants. It shows some attempt to update the setting to the present day. That alone will probably get me to pick up Secrets of the Covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:13:41-08:00","id":1017602,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sinister elders hiding in the shadows&quot; is totally a thing Requiem has shitloads of. They're just so in the shadows the books never directly mention them. Like whoever the hell is pulling the strings of Task Force: VALKYRIE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:42:32-08:00","id":1017623,"title":"","content":"You can always use Requiem's mechanics and combine it with Masquerade's metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:44:19-08:00","id":1017625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017602#post1017602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Sinister elders hiding in the shadows&amp;quot; is totally a thing Requiem has shitloads of. They're just so in the shadows the books never directly mention them. Like whoever the hell is pulling the strings of Task Force: VALKYRIE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abraham Lincoln, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T07:17:36-08:00","id":1017638,"title":"","content":"Yep, it's a running joke made almost semi canon by virtue of how it caught up that its good ol' Abe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T07:49:20-08:00","id":1017649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017638#post1017638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, it's a running joke made almost semi canon by virtue of how it caught up that its good ol' Abe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big part of why that particular bit of fanon is so popular is due to the fact that it kind of redeems TFV as hunters. It's hard to feel like your character is a candle against the darkness when you know your character works for an organization that's canonically the puppets of a vampire conspiracy. But if the vampire pulling the strings is a historical figure and the subject of a cult film in which he's a vampire hunter, it doesn't feel so bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:07:14-08:00","id":1017652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017649#post1017649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a big part of why that particular bit of fanon is so popular is due to the fact that it kind of redeems TFV as hunters. It's hard to feel like your character is a candle against the darkness when you know your character works for an organization that's canonically the puppets of a vampire conspiracy. But if the vampire pulling the strings is a historical figure and the subject of a cult film in which he's a vampire hunter, it doesn't feel so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Though to be fair to the Task Force Valkyrie, most of the conspiracies are fucked and subverted anyways, so it's not like they're uniquely fucked in this situation. I mean, Cheiron Corp is led by eldritch abominations,the Knights of Saint George work for the Abyss, the Knights of Saint Adrian work for an Angel and the Malleus Malleficarum's leader is a ghoul.<br /> <br /> Abraham Lincoln being the one to lead the Task Force is awesome though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:21:03-08:00","id":1017662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017649#post1017649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big part of why that particular bit of fanon is so popular is due to the fact that it kind of redeems TFV as hunters. It's hard to feel like your character is a candle against the darkness when you know your character works for an organization that's canonically the puppets of a vampire conspiracy. But if the vampire pulling the strings is a historical figure and the subject of a cult film in which he's a vampire hunter, it doesn't feel so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try telling that to the Hunter forum. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires\">Apparently Task Force Valkyrie is ruined</a> if there's a vampire involved anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:23:58-08:00","id":1017664,"title":"","content":"I feel like we see this thread every time we see buzz around new books. but anyways. Check out Chicago by Night one of the first source books for masquerade. It doesn't have a world shattering / conquest of conspiracy. It's a very basic elder vs elder from ancient Greece. Between Menele and Helena are the main pushers of the plot. And they play out their wars in Proxy characters. Thrown in with some romance between a few minor characters.<br /> <br /> Which actually makes me think; That a lot of the vision or early intent of the material was a retelling of Greek/Roman gods, but with a dark gothic kick to it. I mean you have ancient and powerful nigh immortal beings dicking over modern 'heros' . I use the Terms heros not in the moral sense but in the larger then life character sense.<br /> <br /> So getting back to the point: Metaplot is what you make it. I personally disliked the later gonzo world spanning my explosion is bigger than your spirit nuke setting shattering nonsense. but the early drama plays are golden material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:45:02-08:00","id":1017732,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing. I liked the Chicago citybooks and the adventure Under a Blood Red Moon - really one of the earliest examples of metaplot, and one I wish Requiem would imitate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:48:07-08:00","id":1017734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017732#post1017732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing. I liked the Chicago citybooks and the adventure Under a Blood Red Moon - really one of the earliest examples of metaplot, and one I wish Requiem would imitate.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've already got Masquerade for metaplot, no need to make Requiem more like its predecessor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:54:13-08:00","id":1017740,"title":"","content":"Well I can certainly sympathize JulianMoon, although more because we're sort of photo negatives of each other. For years I'd tried to either change or remove elements of the metaplot from my Masquerade projects, but to little avail as 90% of the players were frustratingly versed in it. (That is, of course, until Requiem 2nd Edition descended from evil heaven and I had no reason to play Masquerade ever again.)<br /> <br /> But as I said I sympathize with your plight, and beyond the recommendations already made, Danse Macabre is an excellent choice although I'd also add Damnation City for the city examples and Prince archetypes, one series of books I highly recommend you read if you want to craft a Requiem metaplot is Mummy the Curse. And I know, it's a strange suggestion, but here me out:<br /> <br /> Mummy the Curse is a game about truly immortal and impossibly old monsters who were created by Gods(ish?) and were once the blessed and favored servants in the first true empire the world had ever seen, so old now that no trace or evidence of it's existence remains. They survived their Empire's collapse and to these very nights manipulate fanatical cults and shape society in accordance to the old Gods and possess near god-like powers themselves, but so much of their memories have eroded away that some only have the cause left to fight for without even knowing why. This would be a great template for the Methuselahs of your metaplot, and Irem can serve as a great template for how your own First City could have operated. And most of all, it showcases the dangers of fading memory and lies. As the truth behind the Nameless Empire is only known to the ST and not the players, so the Arisen discover their horrible past alongside their players who learn just how terrible the cause they fight for is. Not unlike the Jyhad itself, where ancient grudges have played out for so long that the reason behind them would probably spark another Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> And that all I've got. Good luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T12:28:39-08:00","id":1017752,"title":"","content":"Though I'm as against the metaplot as a thing in the books as most here, I'm not against chronicles based in complex, world-and-beyond-spanning plots.<br /> <br /> So, I can personally do two things. To help development of such, and to suggest mythologies. World mythologies are fairly rich and can serve as the beginning of a &quot;meta-plot&quot;. Choose a few and decide they're mostly remnants of a true past, like the fragments of Nod. Use contradictory versions as a bonus on that. This should give you plenty material to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T12:53:49-08:00","id":1017762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017623#post1017623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can always use Requiem's mechanics and combine it with Masquerade's metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely what my group does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:16:51-08:00","id":1017769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017732#post1017732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing. I liked the Chicago citybooks and the adventure Under a Blood Red Moon - really one of the earliest examples of metaplot, and one I wish Requiem would imitate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under a Blood Red Moon is actually just plot, on account of being an adventure.<br /> <br /> Now, Chicago by Night 2nd edition being published with particular outcomes to Under a Blood Red Moon qualifies as metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:03:38-08:00","id":1017782,"title":"","content":"I think oftentimes people who say they want &quot;more metaplot&quot; in Requiem aren't necessarily looking for setting and plot details to change from one release to the next. More, they are often looking for setting and plot elements that operate on a grander scale, or that interact more directly with the real world, or more clearly defined setting and plot details. Most of them probably want some combination of all of the above. But I think that gets lost when it's all lumped into &quot;metaplot&quot; and the folks who don't want Clans suddenly being allied to different factions or swapping out Disciplines, or suffering mass hysteria because their Antediluvian was killed when a new book comes out say to get that shit away from our Requiem. A lot of what folks want out of Masquerade's plot can be adapted to Requiem without the Meta part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:55:30-08:00","id":1017810,"title":"","content":"Internally, I divide this kind of detail into three categories:<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory and sample settings: </b>Although 1e started with a light touch on these, we started going backstory-and-example-heavy in 2007 with <i>Requiem for Rome</i> and then the clanbooks. At the time, this &quot;metaplot&quot; was controversial. But now, we've got <i>Dark Eras</i> and everything!<br /> <br /> <b>Fiction arcs:</b> See the Chicago story arcs, and the glass armonium/patron storyline in the clanbooks. This stuff moves forward linearly, but does not impact the setting. Chicago tends to update when I work with Greg Stolze.<br /> <br /> <b>Change over time (what I usually call metaplot):</b> This is New Orleans-only, for various historical development reasons. The Katrina/Week of Nightmares story in the clanbooks moved New Orleans materially forward along with current events. <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> revisits Vidal in the present day, visibly changed by those stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 12-16-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T15:56:10-08:00","id":1017835,"title":"","content":"It seems for everyone who likes the addition of metaplot there's another who hates its inclusion.<br /> <br /> I always viewed it as a big combined story. Just one we don't see much of. Perhaps its due to my penchant for comics and their universes, where characters that once existed can seem not to exist, until they do again and a writers lack of inclusion of a character doesn't mean they never existed. And that allows me to imagine what's happening and put them in or alter them accordingly, as a toolbox does. I appreciate in a lot of things, aspects of the background like El Abominar in Belial's Brood or the UK's beshilu and their organized religion are just meant to be that, fodder for plots that you can do with as thou wilt, but I've never had much problem combining it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:12:31-08:00","id":1017908,"title":"","content":"A &quot;metaplot&quot; is a combination of things.<br /> <br /> In those cases, I dare to say that people aren't necessarily wanting a grander scale (though it can be a part of it), nor a change over time (though it adds a sense of density). I doubt it have to do with relating to real life in any way, though it fits the setting of CoD, anyway.<br /> <br /> What I think they want is self-reference. Is to new material complement older material. Is to tidbits in Book B highlight elements that cross over back to Book A, so you get a sense of connection, of a greater background and maybe some major stories forming through the minor ones told.<br /> <br /> Maybe it could be a good idea to offer a book of ideas on how to link elements to create a &quot;metaplot&quot;, with some examples. It wouldn't substitute a true metaplot for whomever want it, but would certainly be a start, and a good addition by itself (since we can still make use of it on our games. We <u>can</u> have a metaplot on our games).<br /> <br /> The last element, the sensation of an author creating a big material for you to learn and explore, that won't be done, period. But maybe some lines of Novels and such could do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:37:26-08:00","id":1017916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017740#post1017740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I can certainly sympathize JulianMoon, although more because we're sort of photo negatives of each other. For years I'd tried to either change or remove elements of the metaplot from my Masquerade projects, but to little avail as 90% of the players were frustratingly versed in it. (That is, of course, until Requiem 2nd Edition descended from evil heaven and I had no reason to play Masquerade ever again.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually yeah this. I was talking to a few of my old GMs. GM1 hated working in established settings. Because he felt like players kept trying to drag in parts of the metaplot that were irrelevant. Like the old question &quot;Why doesn't Elminster just do / hasn't just done [blank]?&quot; Why because it's YOUR STORY not some level30 npc. If the world's problems could easily be solved we wouldn't need brave adventures to save the day. And thus in conflict and struggle we find the story and pathos. It's Dungeons and Dragons Not Bankers and Bondsmen. GM2 c<span style=\"font-family:arial\">ommented that it felt like backseat gming. With the players writing the setting but its the St who has to run it.<br /> <br /> I'm somewhere in the middle. I know that having a background setting is good backdrop to work with and know where it's going. But it should be the backdrop, and not overshadow the story's conflict. Gone with the Wind is a really good example of this Its the story of a woman living in the before and after the Civil War. The War happens but it isn't the central conflict of the story. But you know how many stories have dissolved in front of a larger metaplot?<br /> <br /> And mainly, It's a lot harder to take something away from players once they've got it. If you're constantly having to take things out of the meta. Folks will be non too displeased. And I believe we all know that one guy who'd use metaknowledge. which is otherwise still distasteful. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  Spelling 12-15-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:43:19-08:00","id":1017919,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, there's nothing stopping you from having your own huge figures controlling everything, with plots that change over time, and such-like. But such things shouldn't become so all-encompassing that it becomes difficult to run the game without them. You can run a game in New Orleans without having Vidal around, or in Montreal without the Nameless, without players going &quot;But they Vidal is Prince!&quot; or &quot;But the Nameless keeps that from happening!&quot;. Those are optional settings, and other fluff might reference them, but the game doesn't RELY on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:32:03-08:00","id":1019303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1017585-requiem-and-masquerade?p=1017649#post1017649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a big part of why that particular bit of fanon is so popular is due to the fact that it kind of redeems TFV as hunters. It's hard to feel like your character is a candle against the darkness when you know your character works for an organization that's canonically the puppets of a vampire conspiracy. But if the vampire pulling the strings is a historical figure and the subject of a cult film in which he's a vampire hunter, it doesn't feel so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abe Lincoln as a vampire hunter who kept up the struggle even after his Embrace, and has an entire government task force to help him out, is pretty cool. Part of me feels like, if Abe really is an elder, that Washington is vampire-free thanks to his vigilance. Heck, I'm even willing to entertain the idea that VII is a Covenant he made himself. After all, his most famous speech starts off with &quot;four score and <b>seven </b>years ago.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for metaplot, there are enough threads in some of the books that you can get a picture of what's happening in a city, but there's nothing stopping you from using the fluff in one book, not using any other books, and extrapolating out a progression of events from there to the present day. Or, you know, ignore the fluff for a setting. Onyx Path isn't going to issue a cease-and-desist order on you for saying that the Nameless never showed up in Montreal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}